### SKILL.md  [instructions]
-   Book of the Day — a daily book oracle inspired by fortune cookies. Use this skill when the user asks for "book of the day", "today's book", "今日之书", "书签运势", "再抽一次", or similar. One uplifting book per draw, a fortune archetype, and a light poetic reading — never heavy or negative. When the user says "再抽一次", request again with &redraw=1 to get a different book. Respond in the user's language.
- Request today's book from the skill's source (use `BOOK_OF_THE_DAY_API_URL` from config if set, otherwise `https://book-of-the-day.vercel.app`): `GET {URL}/?date=YYYY-MM-DD` (omit `date` for today). For "再抽一次" (draw again), append `&redraw=1` to get a **different book**. You receive a book object with `title`, `author`, `topics`, `rating`, `description`, `archetype`, `cover_url`. Use it for the steps below.
- Offer a light "draw again" option (再抽一次). When the user asks for it, **request again with `&redraw=1`** appended to the URL — this returns a **different book**. Produce the full reading for that new book.
- - Default (no redraw): same book for everyone each calendar day. With `&redraw=1`: a different book each time
+   Book of the Day — a daily book oracle inspired by fortune cookies. Use this skill when the user asks for "book of the day", "today's book", "今日之书", "书签运势", "再抽一次", or similar. Each request returns a different book (每个人不一样，再抽一次也不同). One uplifting book per draw, a fortune archetype, and a light poetic reading. Respond in the user's language.
+ `GET {URL}/?date=YYYY-MM-DD` (omit `date` for today). **Each request returns a different book** — different people get different books, and "再抽一次" (draw again) gets a different book. When the user says "再抽一次", make a **new request**; do NOT reuse the previous book. Never say "同一本书" (same book).
+ Source: `BOOK_OF_THE_DAY_API_URL` from config, or `https://book-of-the-day.vercel.app`. Response: `title`, `author`, `topics`, `rating`, `description`, `archetype`, `cover_url`.
+ Offer a "draw again" option (再抽一次). When the user asks for it: **make a NEW request** (same URL `/?date=...`). Each request returns a different book — do NOT reuse the previous book. Produce the full reading for the new book.
+ - Each request returns a different book — different people, different draws